The market resolves to Yes if the specified person receives a presidential pardon, commutation, or reprieve during the specified Presidential term and before the deadline date.

For purposes of this Contract, a member of Trump's Cabinet refers to the Vice President and any official listed as a member of the Cabinet on the White House's Cabinet page at the time of the pardon. A pardon counts even if the recipient has not been charged with a crime, even if the recipient rejects it, and even if it covers the recipient by role, agency, or policy area without naming them.

The following do NOT count:
grants made before Issuance, including Proclamation 10989 of Nov 7, 2025;
grants that cover the recipient only by describing conduct, without naming them or their role, agency, or policy area;
pardons granted after the recipient has left the Cabinet;
officials serving in an acting capacity, even if listed on the White House's Cabinet page;
state pardons.
